      "text": "Interplanetary mission design is the art of finding trajectories from Earth to a target body that satisfy constraints on launch vehicle capability, mission duration, spacecraft mass, and arrival conditions. The fundamental tool is the patched conic approximation; the gold standard is full numerical integration."
